-- R32 - DOWNGRADE NEEDS A PRIMARY CHECK: the accuracy gate may correct, strike or tag a figure credited to an
-- official release or a named wire only after reading that source; an older story never corrects a newer one.
-- Source: thread "Act on Neon feedback for Takeaways", 22 Nov 2026 (owner forwarded Gemini Neon's review). Checked at
-- the primary sources: the Opus run struck Taiwan's 21 Nov short-sale ban, Reuters' 20 Nov Nvidia accounting story,
-- ABS October jobs and China's October gold imports; the Fable run also tagged the ABS figures unverified.
-- Proposed 22 Nov 2026 with dash.propose_rule and put in force the same morning (10:19 SGT) with
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid in ('R32','R33') and status = 'proposed';
-- so the Mon 23 Nov runs read it. "revert R32" removes it. The call below is the exact call that was run.
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "A figure or event credited to an official release or a named wire is checked at that source before it is corrected, struck or tagged unverified; an older story never corrects a newer one", "body": "DOWNGRADE NEEDS A PRIMARY CHECK (review of the 21 and 22 Nov 2026 digests: the accuracy gate struck four real items). Applies to STEP 3D (ACCURACY GATE), its adversarial pass, the PLAUSIBILITY GATE and the completeness sweep.\n\n1. SCOPE. Any number or event that a feed credits to an official body (statistics office, customs, central bank, regulator, ministry, exchange) or to a named wire or paper (Reuters, Bloomberg, WSJ, FT, Nikkei, Yonhap, SCMP).\n\n2. CHECK BEFORE ANY DOWNGRADE. Before such an item is corrected, struck, removed from a section, stripped of an arrow or tagged \"[unverified]\" / \"[source claim — unverified]\", the run opens, in order, until one answers: (a) the issuer's own release page for that date, with WebFetch, or with the Exa tool web_fetch_exa when WebFetch is absent (abs.gov.au, customs.gov.cn / english.customs.gov.cn, fsc.gov.tw, cbc.gov.tw, the central bank's press page); (b) a search restricted to the issuer's domain with the figure (\"site:<domain> <figure>\"), Exa web_search_exa or WebSearch; (c) the wire headline with its date, read through any outlet that syndicates or quotes it. numbers.tsv records the URL read for every downgraded or corrected row.\n\n3. OUTCOMES. CONFIRMED: keep it and cite the primary. CONTRADICTED: correct it only when the contradicting source is the issuer or a wire AND is dated the same day as the claim or later. An older story never corrects a newer one: a 17 Nov report cannot correct a 20 Nov report, and a rule announced 19 Nov cannot correct a separate announcement of 21 Nov. NOT FOUND after (a) to (c): keep the item, tag it \"[unconfirmed — checked <where>]\", let it carry a single arrow at most, never strike it. \"The data I have runs only to an earlier month\" and \"not found\" are never a correction.\n\n4. FOOTER. The accuracy gate line adds \"· downgrades primary-checked D of D\"; any downgrade not checked counts against D and is named.\n\n5. CARRIED CORRECTIONS (checked by hand on 22 Nov 2026 at the primary; restore each in the next run where still relevant, then drop this part): (i) Taiwan FSC release of Sat 21 Nov 2026 (fsc.gov.tw, dataserno 202611210001): five measures from Mon 23 Nov: a market-wide ban on margin and borrowed-share short sales below the previous close (broker and futures-dealer hedging exempt), minimum short-sale margin 130% to 150%, no new put-warrant listings, buybacks encouraged, lenders asked to stop lending and recall shares. It is a new step beyond the 20 Nov rule that covered only stocks down 3.5% or more; the 22 Nov Opus run wrongly struck it as already in force. (ii) ABS Labour Force, October 2026, released 19 Nov: unemployment 4.9% (September 4.7%; ABS calls it a 0.1-point rise on unrounded data, the highest since October 2021), employment -43,500. (iii) China customs data of Fri 20 Nov (reported by SCMP): October imports of unwrought non-monetary gold 155.85 t, +174.1% y/y, US$20.73bn, the third-largest import by value. (iv) Reuters, Fri 20 Nov, two sources: SEC enforcement staff are examining Nvidia's accounting practices; the accounting focus is new against the WSJ report of 17 Nov, which could not establish the probe's focus.", "rationale": "Gemini Neon's review of 22 Nov 2026 said the Opus run downgraded three real primary releases in two days. Checked at the primary sources on 22 Nov: all three were real, and a fourth was worse. The 21 Nov Opus gate 'corrected' Reuters' Nvidia accounting probe to the older WSJ disclosure framing and tagged the ABS October jobs figures unverified; the 22 Nov Opus gate stripped China's customs gold imports of their arrow because 'WGC data run only to September', and struck Taiwan's new short-sale ban (announced 21 Nov, in force 23 Nov) by matching it to the narrower 19-20 Nov curbs, so Monday's biggest Asia policy change left the Opus digest. The Opus run printed 'Primary pages 0/25 fetched (no direct page-fetch tool this run)' although the Exa connector is attached to its task. The Fable run also tagged the ABS figures unverified on 22 Nov. Common cause: a search-only adversarial pass treats an older or narrower story, or its own missing data, as a contradiction. The digest prompts are at their byte cap, so the fix goes in as a rule.", "evidence": "Gmail: Opus 21 Nov (1a1fb55fa490e106) and 22 Nov (1a2007420fbaba0a) footers, Fable 22 Nov (1a2006064e565f05) ledger; primary pages read 22 Nov: fsc.gov.tw release 202611210001, abs.gov.au Labour Force October 2026, SCMP 20 Nov customs story, Bloomberg/Quartz carrying Reuters 20 Nov.", "revert_if": "Revert if, over two weeks, a figure kept under this rule as unconfirmed proves false in a card's thesis, or if the check adds more than five minutes to a run on two days.", "review_due": "2026-12-20", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
